Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:34:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 082/123] CLIs: report errors on stderr, never in a message box

proxmoxbackup-directory and proxmoxbackup-machine showed a Windows
message box (dialog.Error) for missing options and when another backup
job held the process lock. From Task Scheduler, a service or any other
unattended run the box waits for a click nobody gives, so the job hangs
instead of failing. directorybackup also carried on after the
missing-options box with the invalid configuration, because only the
non-Windows branch exited.

Both programs now print the message to stderr and exit non-zero on every
platform: 1 for missing or invalid options (followed by the option
list), 2 when another job is running, as before. Exit codes are what a
scheduler can act on.

The message boxes inside machinebackuplib (disk open failures) are left
alone here, since the GUI shares that code.

Tested on Windows 10: both programs, run with no options and with the
process lock held by another process, print to stderr and exit 1 and 2
without opening a window. Vet and build clean for windows and linux;
directorybackup tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JSSBMF6hRk92jsHCMKgDRx
Upstream: tizbac/proxmoxbackupclient_go@922cba81935def0021f848288c0aecec539ead1f
---
 directorybackup/main.go | 23 ++++++++---------------
 machinebackup/main.go   | 20 ++++++--------------
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 29 deletions(-)

diff --git a/directorybackup/main.go b/directorybackup/main.go
index e87b6ad..6f218f1 100644
--- a/directorybackup/main.go
+++ b/directorybackup/main.go
@@ -13,7 +13,6 @@ import (
 	"os"
 	"path/filepath"
 	"pbscommon"
-	"runtime"
 	"snapshot"
 	"strings"
 	"sync"
@@ -21,7 +20,6 @@ import (
 	"time"
 
 	"github.com/alphadose/haxmap"
-	"github.com/tawesoft/golib/v2/dialog"
 )
 
 var defaultMailSubjectTemplate = "Backup {{.Status}}"
@@ -170,19 +168,14 @@ func main() {
 
 	cfg := loadConfig()
 
+	// Errors go to stderr with a non-zero exit, never a message box: a box
+	// waits for a click that an unattended scheduled run never gets (and on
+	// Windows the run used to carry on after it with the invalid options).
 	if ok := cfg.valid(); !ok {
-		if runtime.GOOS == "windows" {
-			usage := "All options are mandatory:\n"
-			flag.VisitAll(func(f *flag.Flag) {
-				usage += "-" + f.Name + " " + f.Usage + "\n"
-			})
-			_ = dialog.Error(usage)
-		} else {
-			fmt.Println("All options are mandatory")
-
-			flag.PrintDefaults()
-			os.Exit(1)
-		}
+		fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, "Missing or invalid options. Options:")
+		flag.CommandLine.SetOutput(os.Stderr)
+		flag.PrintDefaults()
+		os.Exit(1)
 	}
 
 	// Without -certfingerprint, fetch the fingerprint the server presents and
@@ -208,7 +201,7 @@ func main() {
 	lock_ok := L.AcquireProcessLock()
 	if !lock_ok {
 
-		_ = dialog.Error("Backup jobs need to run exclusively, please wait until the previous job has finished")
+		fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, "Another backup job is running; backup jobs run one at a time. Try again when it has finished.")
 		os.Exit(2)
 	}
 	defer L.ReleaseProcessLock()
diff --git a/machinebackup/main.go b/machinebackup/main.go
index 0e8d970..4a02500 100644
--- a/machinebackup/main.go
+++ b/machinebackup/main.go
